{
  "_comment": "The contract the digest and raw pages' vote script speaks to /api/vote (src/cyris/adapters/output/templates/_promote_script.html.j2, _probe_script.html.j2), answered the same by both editions. workers/app/test/vote_contract.test.js holds the app Worker (workers/app/src/router.js, handleVote) and the promote Worker behind it (workers/promote/src/index.js) to every case, and reads what each accepted vote left in the promote queue; tests/test_local_votes.py holds a local `cyris triage-ui` (TriageServer) on a SQLite file to the same cases and reads the stamped row. `verdict` is the state the vote sets on its article once applied, `accepted` or `rejected`, or null for a request that queues and stamps nothing. A case whose `url` is not `stored` names an article the store lacks: the cloud edition queues it and its sync stamps nothing (`apply_promotions`), so the local one answers the same and writes no row. docs/decisions/0044-a-local-install-takes-votes.md",
